# Unified UI

Reuse existing patterns. Do not invent a new control style for the same action.

## Edit / delete / close

Destructive and edit actions are **round icon buttons**, never full-width text buttons.

- Use `IconToolbar` + `IconButton` from `src/components/IconToolbar.tsx`.
- Trash = `IconButton danger` with `Trash2`.
- Edit = `IconButton` with `Pencil`.
- Close = `IconButton` with `X`.
- On a full page, put them in `page-toolbar` opposite the back button.
- On a sheet, put them in `IconToolbar` at the top-end (same as the schedule class sheet).
- Confirm destructive actions before deleting.

## Forms

Stack fields the way the add-class sheet does:

- Label above the control, aligned to the start (RTL-aware, not hardcoded `text-align: right`).
- Compact steppers (`+/−`) for numbers and time; the value in the middle stays keyboard-editable.
- Selects are full-width dropdowns, not scattered chip grids.
- Related fields (time + capacity) sit in a two-column row.

## Lists

- Selectable people/items are checkbox rows, not unlabeled chips.
- Delete-from-roster stays behind an explicit “edit list” mode, not an always-visible X on each row.

## Back navigation

Use `BackButton` from `src/components/IconToolbar.tsx` with an explicit `to` parent route.
Never `navigate(-1)` in nested flows (library → lesson → builder → exercises), or back will reopen the previous nested screen.

- Prefer CSS classes over inline styles.
- Prefer logical CSS (`inset-inline`, `margin-inline`, `text-align: start`) so Hebrew RTL and English LTR both work.
- Accent color is purple (`#8b5cf6` / `#a78bfa`), not the browser default blue.
